# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually copies.
#
# target/ dominates a locally built checkout by three orders of
# magnitude in file count. BuildKit walks the whole context before it
# copies anything, so leaving it in costs every local build and buys
# nothing — the Dockerfile only takes Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and src/.
#
# This used to be covered by onym-infra's rsync excludes, which no
# longer apply now that deploys build these contexts directly rather
# than on the droplet (onymchat/onym-infra#13).
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT an input: published/ and manifest/ are
# read at runtime from a mount, not built in. The published terms must
# be the bytes the deployment serves and signs, not a copy frozen into
# an image at build time.
.git/
target/

# Excluded even though the Dockerfile copies none of them — a build
# context is the wrong place for a signing seed to be sitting when
# someone later reaches for `COPY . .`.
secrets/
*.p8
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
*.log
